{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0214", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-etale}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cf6f8a62a78b069129b5d383799e448636220c05eabec396741a5f2490b8e534", "source_text": "The <ACCENT_0001>tale topology", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5470b4e9df438e64ff5833f78aa27e2d5a6dcae40ca973584fb4b470fe6ea8bf", "unit_id": "tag:0214:title"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0214", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3373d69d1a771d1b240d3f94798edce7e161caf54de4b2de49dd8524c8dc1502", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e5a472a4571308e3994a965930d7c6b9176dc06bf7bc67a17f4bf80fed40062b", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a scheme. We would like to define the <ACCENT_0001>tale-topology on\nthe category of schemes over <MATH_0002>. According to our general principle\nwe first introduce the notion of an <ACCENT_0002>tale covering.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:84df789fe60b2360f37ae1eee6343e4874d625441dd3093e8f6875a0e127221f", "unit_id": "tag:0214:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0214", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$T$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{f_i : T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0004": "$f_i$", "MATH_0005": "$T = \\bigcup f_i(T_i)$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-etale-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:283f9dea2be6a5f99e7e729bc3db42e6c914a1813f97c1b0e20c1ac32623e25a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a6554c6fe402dd002fc54e9b2844a3a33feed7cc35a7b36a58157be090eb3e07", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. An <TEXTITOPEN_0001><ACCENT_0001>tale covering of <MATH_0002><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is a family\nof morphisms <MATH_0003> of schemes\nsuch that each <MATH_0004> is <ACCENT_0002>tale and such that <MATH_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e5ab86b0d4a08fa11eef05899663266999ae830c539f36de14d2edee212343f8", "unit_id": "tag:0215:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0214", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-zariski-etale}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:634c67e9fca572c91652b33989f8ac44edf62d5184b3ed48ec772843d0e19542", "source_text": "Any Zariski covering is an <ACCENT_0001>tale covering.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:14e5f0673c4ca70ba01f59403030e111b476623c4b1d9b5efc45527632643802", "unit_id": "tag:0216:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0214", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-open-immersion-etale}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0268bac827646a6fe8270ddcfcfeb09919e5f5bfc9b025d5e21137adbdbedd57", "source_text": "This is clear from the definitions and the fact that an open immersion\nis an <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism, see\nMorphisms, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:51395a7ed8d23ac999425bbefb6b23aeb3a4e9c10f62d22fc8663798a706eb41", "unit_id": "tag:0216:proof"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0214", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-definition-site}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:74d5d4f34a327c0d6f075040829b93a4547462492cb35da320bb755a4aa57fde", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNext, we show that this notion satisfies the conditions of\nSites, Definition <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fe60d7ff7dec91903335c151eda3e3489f64647b495bf10d622c43cc9afc0c89", "unit_id": "tag:0214:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0214", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0004": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0005": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0006": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$T' \\to T$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{T' \\to T\\}$", "MATH_0004": "$T$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$i$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{T_{ij} \\to T_i\\}_{j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{T_{ij} \\to T\\}_{i \\in I, j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0010": "$T' \\to T$", "MATH_0011": "$\\{T' \\times_T T_i \\to T'\\}_{i\\in I}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-etale}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9e2cfe153eb45f4e05511defe14a0d0d67a3d5c22cf50aff12afe0aee9a4b79d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c2d14009b4eca1e17a8512657a487ddf3edfab215736e2484ec8b11d2b4cb2b9", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0002> is an isomorphism then <MATH_0003>\nis an <ACCENT_0001>tale covering of <MATH_0004>.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0005> is an <ACCENT_0002>tale covering and for each\n<MATH_0006> we have an <ACCENT_0003>tale covering <MATH_0007>, then\n<MATH_0008> is an <ACCENT_0004>tale covering.\n<STRUCT_0004> If <MATH_0009> is an <ACCENT_0005>tale covering\nand <MATH_0010> is a morphism of schemes then\n<MATH_0011> is an <ACCENT_0006>tale covering.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d9c6ef7eae0e23c941e0705a56bba8595e473ee2567e4d6f94942c984207b617", "unit_id": "tag:0217:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0214", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:df3039757d5a364b62c2f72f185f78dc01436b1e906c1c5fe6e0df286bbdffd3", "source_text": "Omitted.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:872a8cfa74892c6e6464bd864d9f1c292f4f523caba3e51ac3dafbfc84db48f6", "unit_id": "tag:0217:proof"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0214", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$T$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{U_j \\to T\\}_{j = 1, \\ldots, m}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$U_j$", "MATH_0007": "$U_j$", "MATH_0008": "$T_i$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-etale-affine}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:70f5bcb2ae6ec87aa1fc2d0b5609686c27090116cc9aa3e1bd5d33260e5c7028", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4cda840b3fafbda5cf8ad78f4eae51e079bad71d4d85e51dc35ac19bfea8535c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an affine scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an <ACCENT_0001>tale covering of <MATH_0003>.\nThen there exists an <ACCENT_0002>tale covering\n<MATH_0004> which is a refinement\nof <MATH_0005> such that each <MATH_0006> is an affine\nscheme. Moreover, we may choose each <MATH_0007> to be open affine\nin one of the <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1c2e20a7d0f9355044f87b6b3743f0dffbda1789895c42592b647b747b8a7d50", "unit_id": "tag:0218:statement"}
